---
import { hackingPrizePost } from '../../../data/blog'
import ArticleLayout from '../../../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro'

const withdrawalDate = new Date(hackingPrizePost.updatedAt)
const dateFormat = { dateStyle: 'long', timeZone: 'UTC' } as const
const publishedDate = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en', dateFormat).format(withdrawalDate)
const publishedDateCzech = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('cs-CZ', dateFormat).format(withdrawalDate)
---

<ArticleLayout {...hackingPrizePost} eyebrow="Withdrawal notice">
  <div class="article-callout">
    <p><strong>Published <time datetime={hackingPrizePost.updatedAt}>{publishedDate}</time></strong></p>
    <p>
      Authier hereby withdraws its public promise of a Litecoin reward for the
      vault decryption challenge, including all previously advertised amounts.
      The withdrawal takes effect upon publication of this notice.
    </p>
    <p>
      This withdrawal does not affect any rights protected by Section 2885(2)
      of the Czech Civil Code. If you completed qualifying work in reliance on
      the offer before you knew or should have known of the withdrawal, contact
      <a href="mailto:security@authier.pm">security@authier.pm</a> with the
      details and when you completed the work. The security disclosure policy
      continues to apply.
    </p>
    <div lang="cs">
      <p><strong>Oznámení o odvolání veřejného příslibu odměny</strong></p>
      <p>
        Authier tímto odvolává veřejný příslib odměny v litecoinech za prokázání
        úplného dešifrování trezoru Authier, včetně všech dříve zveřejněných
        výší odměny. Odvolání nabývá účinnosti zveřejněním tohoto oznámení
        <time datetime={hackingPrizePost.updatedAt}>{publishedDateCzech}</time>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Práva chráněná podle § 2885 odst. 2 občanského zákoníku tímto odvoláním
        nejsou dotčena. Pokud jste výkon splňující tehdejší podmínky provedli se
        zřetelem k příslibu a v té době jste o odvolání nevěděli ani nemuseli
        vědět, napište na <a href="mailto:security@authier.pm">security@authier.pm</a>
        a uveďte podrobnosti a dobu dokončení.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <details class="prize-archive">
    <summary>Archived article and terms (withdrawn)</summary>
    <p>
      The article body below is preserved as it last appeared. Earlier
      announcements listed other reward amounts.
    </p>
    <p>
      A password manager earns trust by standing up to scrutiny. Today, we are
      putting a reward behind that idea: <strong>hack Authier and receive 8 LTC
      (Litecoin)</strong>. The challenge is specific: fully decrypt a user's stored
      vault secrets and demonstrate the attack programmatically.
    </p>

    <aside class="prize-card" aria-label="Hacking prize requirements">
      <p class="prize-label">The reward</p>
      <p class="prize-amount">8 <span>LTC</span></p>
      <p class="prize-requirement">
        Full decryption of stored secrets.<br />
        Reproducible, programmatic proof.
      </p>
      <a href="mailto:security@authier.pm">Submit to security@authier.pm →</a>
    </aside>

    <h2>What counts as a successful hack?</h2>
    <p>
      A qualifying submission must show a vulnerability in Authier that lets an
      attacker recover the complete plaintext secrets in a user's vault without
      the user's master password, legitimate decryption keys, or normal authorized
      unlock. That includes the secret values stored in the test vault, such as
      passwords and TOTP seeds, rather than only item titles or account metadata.
      The attack must be performed over the network and cannot assume access to
      the vault owner's machine or email account.
    </p>
    <p>
      Getting a copy of encrypted data, bypassing a login screen, or showing a
      screenshot of a claimed compromise does not by itself meet this challenge.
      The result must be <strong>full decryption of stored secrets</strong>, with
      working code that demonstrates how the attacker gets there.
    </p>
    <p>
      To qualify for the reward, the vulnerability must still be reproducible on
      the latest commit of
      <a href="https://github.com/authier-pm/authier/tree/main">Authier's <code>main</code> branch on GitHub</a>
      when you submit your report.
    </p>

    <h2>Show it in code</h2>
    <p>
      Send a runnable proof of concept that we can reproduce independently. A
      script, automated test, or small program is welcome. Include:
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <strong>The setup:</strong> the <code>main</code> commit SHA you tested,
        platform, dependencies, and any access the attacker needs to start.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>The attack:</strong> complete source code and exact commands to
        run it, from the starting conditions through decryption.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>The result:</strong> a test vault containing synthetic secrets,
        with output showing that the program recovered every stored secret
        correctly. Keep the master password and legitimate decryption keys out of
        the attack's inputs.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>The explanation:</strong> the flaw the program exploits and why
        it compromises Authier's protection of stored secrets.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      We will review the report, reproduce the demonstration, and pay the
      <strong>8 LTC reward</strong> for a qualifying, verified full-decryption
      attack. The reward is denominated in Litecoin.
    </p>

    <h2>Research with accounts you control</h2>
    <p>
      Ideally, demonstrate the hack with a <strong>fresh Authier account created
      solely for the hack demo</strong>, populated with synthetic secrets.
    </p>
    <p>
      Use your own test accounts and synthetic secrets, or accounts whose owners
      have explicitly permitted the test. You do not need to expose anyone's real
      passwords to prove that Authier's protections can be broken. Do not access
      other users' data, disrupt the service, or use phishing or social engineering.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our <a href="https://github.com/authier-pm/authier/blob/main/SECURITY.md">vulnerability
      disclosure policy</a> describes the supported versions, scope, and research
      exclusions. Share findings privately and give us time to investigate and
      address them before public disclosure. Other security reports are welcome
      at the same address, even when they do not meet this prize's full-decryption
      requirement.
    </p>

    <h2>Send your submission</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href="mailto:security@authier.pm">security@authier.pm</a> with the
      subject <strong>Authier 8 LTC challenge</strong>, your reproduction
      instructions, and the proof-of-concept source attached or linked privately.
      Use synthetic data in the report. If you want to encrypt your submission,
      the disclosure policy includes our PGP key identifier.
    </p>
    <p>
      Your submission <strong>must include a Litecoin receiving address</strong>
      where we should send the 8 LTC reward if your attack qualifies.
    </p>
    <p>
      Ready to inspect the implementation? Start with the
      <a href="/security">security architecture</a> and the
      <a href="https://github.com/authier-pm/authier">open-source repository</a>.
      We look forward to seeing what you find.
    </p>
  </details>
</ArticleLayout>

<style>
  .prize-archive summary {
    width: fit-content;
    color: var(--accent);
    cursor: pointer;
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  .prize-archive[open] summary {
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }

  .prize-card {
    margin: 38px 0 48px;
    padding: clamp(26px, 5vw, 42px);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-strong);
    border-radius: 18px;
    background:
      radial-gradient(circle at 100% 0, rgba(105, 230, 204, 0.13), transparent 65%),
      var(--surface);
  }

  .prize-card .prize-label {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .prize-card .prize-amount {
    margin: 0 0 20px;
    color: var(--text);
    font-size: clamp(4rem, 12vw, 6rem);
    font-weight: 670;
    letter-spacing: -0.065em;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .prize-amount span {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 0.55em;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  }

  .prize-card .prize-requirement {
    margin-bottom: 22px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .prize-card a {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
</style>
